meta {
  name: Get Product Subpath - Attributes
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/attributes
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.brand: eq Plytix
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account".

  ## What it does
  `GET /products/{id}/attributes` -- returns the product's full
  `attributes` map directly as `data` (same object also embedded under
  `data.attributes` on the plain `GET /products/{id}` request).

  Also confirmed: `GET /products/{id}/attributes/brand` -- 200, returns
  just the single value (`data: "Plytix"`), per `API V3.md`'s
  `attributes/<attribute_name>` subpath.

  ## Subpath discovery technique (applies to every v3 resource)
  Hitting `GET /{resource}/{id}/{path}` with a `{path}` that isn't a
  recognized field/relation returns
  `400 {"errors":[{"name":"ValueError","description":"Field '<path>' not
  found. Available fields: [...]"}]}` -- listing the resource's *raw
  internal model* field names. E.g. for this product:
  `['id','account_id','sku','label','gtin','status','attributes',
  'thumbnail_id','parent_id','num_variations','product_level',
  'product_family_id','product_family_model_id','overwritten_attributes',
  'mark_as_deleted','product_relationships','created','modified',
  'last_context','modified_user_audit','created_user_audit']`.

  **Caveat**: this list is the raw model only -- it does NOT include
  computed/joined relations that are still valid subpaths (`categories`,
  `assets`, `relationships`, all confirmed 200 -- see the sibling
  "Get Product Subpath" requests in this folder). Also note several of
  these raw fields (`product_family_model_id`, `mark_as_deleted`,
  `last_context`, `modified_user_audit`, `created_user_audit`) are **not
  declared anywhere in `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `ProductOutputDto`** -- worth
  a follow-up question to Plytix on whether any are meant to be
  customer-facing. This 400-with-field-list trick is the fastest way to
  discover a resource's real internal fields in later phases -- use it
  before guessing subpath names from the spec alone.
}
